# Shared scan patterns. TRACKED so CI enforces them.
#
# Only patterns that are safe to publish belong here: shapes, not values.
# Anything that is itself sensitive (real names, SSIDs, MAC addresses, the
# WAN IP) goes in scripts/.pii-patterns, which is gitignored and therefore
# only ever applied on a maintainer's machine.
#
# One PCRE per line. Every pattern here must have zero hits on a clean tree,
# otherwise the scan is red by default and stops meaning anything.

# Real SOPS ciphertext. Requires actual base64 after `data:` so the
# documented placeholders (`<encrypted-bytes>`, `...`) do not match.
ENC\[AES256_GCM,data:[A-Za-z0-9+/=]{8,}

# Age recipient public keys.
\bage1[a-z0-9]{58}\b

# Internal service subdomains. The bare apex is the public site and is fine;
# subdomains enumerate the service map.
\b[a-zA-Z0-9-]+\.saltstice\.com\b

# Internal VLAN prefixes. RKE2's own 10.43.0.0/16 is deliberately absent,
# it is identical on every install and redacting it only hurts the writing.
\b10\.10\.[0-9]{1,3}\.
\b192\.168\.1\.
